      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "Given that\n\n$$\ng(-\\sqrt{2})=4,\\,g(\\sqrt{3})=-7,\\,g(4)=-6,\n$$\n\nfind the value of ${g}^{-1}(4).$",
      "worked_solution": "From the given information, we have:\n\n$$\ng(-\\sqrt{2})=4\n$$\n\nApplying ${g}^{-1}$ to both sides of the above equation, and using the fact that ${g}^{-1}(g(x))=x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{-1}(g(-\\sqrt{2})) & ={g}^{-1}(4) \\\\ -\\sqrt{2} & ={g}^{-1}(4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that ${g}^{-1}(4)=-\\sqrt{2}.$",
